# A rule that deletes a bond and writes "." between the two molecules it joined.
#
# "." means the two molecules are still in one complex afterwards, so the rule
# may fire only where something else holds them together.
#
# Open deletes the x-x bond between D and E. The model holds 100 D.E pairs
# joined once, through x (Single), and 100 joined twice, through x and y
# (Ring). On a Single pair the x-x bond is all that holds D and E together, so
# Open must never fire: Single stays at 100. On a Ring pair the y-y bond
# remains, so Open fires and all 100 end up as Opened.
#
# Swap is a control. It moves the bond between F and G from their x sites to
# their y sites, so they stay together through the bond the rule adds. It must
# still fire: all 100 F.G pairs end up as ViaY.
#
# BioNetGen's network generator agrees. Given this model it produces two
# reactions, Open on the Ring pair and Swap, and none on the Single pair.
#
# NFsim did not test "." at all, so Open broke the Single pairs apart too.

begin model
begin parameters
  k  1.0
end parameters
begin molecule types
  D(x,y)
  E(x,y)
  F(x,y)
  G(x,y)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  D(x!1,y).E(x!1,y)       100
  D(x!1,y!2).E(x!1,y!2)   100
  F(x!1,y).G(x!1,y)       100
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  Single  D(x!1,y).E(x!1,y)
  Molecules  Ring    D(x!1,y!2).E(x!1,y!2)
  Molecules  Opened  D(x,y!1).E(x,y!1)
  Molecules  ViaY    F(x,y!1).G(x,y!1)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  Open: D(x!1).E(x!1) -> D(x).E(x)                    k
  Swap: F(x!1,y).G(x!1,y) -> F(x,y!1).G(x,y!1)        k
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
